===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=young male|inh|enm>boye>boy|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|boy//boye|t=servant, commoner, knave, boy}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*bōia|t=boy}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*bōjō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*bōjô|t=younger brother, young male relation}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bō-|t=brother, close male relation}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰā-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰāt-|t=father, elder brother, brother}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|boy|t=boy}}, {{cog|fy|boai|t=boy}}, {{cog|nl|boi|t=boy}}, {{cog|nds|Boi|t=boy}}, and probably to the {{cog|ang|-}} proper name {{m|ang|Bōia}}. Also related to {{cog|vls|boe||brother}}, {{cog|no|-}} dialectal {{m|no|boa||brother}}, {{cog|nl|boef||rogue, knave}}, {{cog|bar|Bua|t=young boy, lad}}, {{cog|de|Bube}} {{gloss|"boy; knave; jack"; > English {{m|en|bub}}}}, {{cog|is|bófi||rogue, crook, bandit, knave}}. See also {{m|en|bully}}.

